# The name behind the recurring `mtk_hal_camera -> default_prop` denial, caught
# live with an uprobe on __system_property_find: `0com.tencent.mm`.  The MTK
# camera stack keeps a hardcoded list of third-party camera apps
# (com.tencent.mm, com.snapchat.android, com.whatsapp, ...) and reads
# `"0" + package` for each one to get per-app tuning.  Every entry starts with
# `com.`, so this single prefix covers the whole family; a digit-first property
# name is legal (init only rejects a leading/trailing dot and `..`), so the
# label is accepted and the read now actually succeeds under enforcing instead
# of hanging the camera path.
0com.                                                       u:object_r:exported_default_prop:s0

